 "title": "Why Most Ads Suck",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator claims that ads suck because creators pitch to the wrong target group. Just like dogs evolved to have human features to please humans, advertisers create ads that appeal to their managers and company bosses to survive and get promoted.",
 "key_points": [
  "Dogs evolved human-like facial features and muscles (LAOM) over generations because humans preferred them, giving them a survival advantage.",
  "The creator worked at an ad agency where his manager explained that the real 'TG' (Target Group) is the client, not the final consumer.",
  "The client's TG is the client's manager, and that manager's TG is their manager, leading up to 50-year-old top company officials.",
  "Agency make money when ideas are approved by the client, not necessarily when the idea is good for consumers.",
  "Ads look like a 50-year-old man's version of Gen Z because the ultimate decision-makers to impress are older company officials.",
  "The creator evolved from pitching ideas he liked to pitching ideas that got approved, resulting in a promotion, comparing it to how dogs evolved."
 ],
 "content": "Why do dogs have facial expressions like us and how the answer to THAT is key to understanding why most Ads fucking suck! but first... why do dogs have human like expressions? Basically it's evolution. Humans preferred dogs with more human like facial features. These dogs were more likely to be fed & protected. Over generations the dogs evolved. They became more like us so we'd like them more. It's a survival advantage. So how the fuck does that explain why most Ads suck? STORY TIME!!!! iske pehle main ek [unclear] kaam karta tha And one day I was pitching a campaign idea for some brand to my manager. I pitched the idea, he rejected it. And then he looked at me with a smile and asked, WHO IS THE T.G? T.G manje Target Group. Brand's target audience. So I told him GENZ, 18-25, Tier 1, Tier 2 city. And then he said, no Chicky, that's not the T.G. And I was like nahi nahi sir, ye dekhiye client ke brief doc me likha hua hai, ye dekhiye. Then he smiled again and said, That's not the T.G. The T.G is the CLIENT. [unclear] my eyes opened. Agency make money not when idea good, but when idea approved. The T.G is the client. But you must be thinking... CLIENT'S T.G -> BRAND'S T.G (a.k.a the consumers). So what difference, they'll approve that only no??? Na, CLIENT'S T.G is CLIENT'S MANAGER. Because CLIENT'S MANAGER decides CLIENT'S appraisal. And the CLIENT'S MANAGER'S T.G is their manager. And it goes deeper and deeper until finally the real T.G are the 50 year old top company officials who everyone wants to impress in the quarterly reviews. You know you see all these supposedly Gen Z ads, jinko banane mein LAKHS AND CRORES kharch kiye gaye hain. But when you see them, they feel like a 50 year old guy's version of what Gen Z's would like. You know why? Because you're not the T.G. The T.G is the CLIENT. It's the ultimate truth & no one can escape it. When I used to work, my T.G was my manager, because my manager would decide my appraisal. In the beginning, I was the kinda guy who'd crack ideas that I'd like to see. And then I evolved and I became the kinda guy who'd crack ideas that would get approved. And then I got promoted. You know, my theory is, just how dogs evolved according to humans, everyone in advertising with each passing day, become more and more like the 50 year olds so that they can survive. Now until one day they wake up and they're like, I want to win awards! And then it's over.",
